# Test: ClassName.new() constructor form.
# Before the fix, Counter.new() returned null because the method-call
# dispatch path did not treat a Value::Class receiver with method "new"
# as a constructor — it fell through to the default "return null" arm.
# After the fix, both Counter() and Counter.new() instantiate the class
# and self-field mutations persist across method calls.
class, Counter
    fn, new()
        set, self.count, 0
        return, self
    /end
    fn, inc()
        set, self.count, self.count + 1
        return, self.count
    /end
/end
set, c, Counter.new()
println, c.inc()
println, c.inc()
println, c.inc()
# Expected output: 1 / 2 / 3
